# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The package is a bash toolkit: a CRLF checkout would break `#!` lines, break
# heredocs and make every `$(...)` capture carry a stray \r. On Windows that
# failure is silent — the files look fine in an editor — so the normalisation is
# pinned here rather than left to a per-machine core.autocrlf setting.
#
# tests/test-package-layout.sh guards this file's presence and its eol=lf rule.
* text=auto eol=lf
